comments.body:
Hi @shivaansh0610-LUFFY, I was looking into this issue as well and traced the current remote build path a bit. --output is currently explicitly blocked for remote builds, and BuildOutputs is not passed through the build API.
I also checked the existing export paths. containers.Export() already streams a merged container rootfs, so one possible approach seems to be: build remotely, create a temporary container from the resulting image, stream its rootfs back using the existing export API, then handle type=local / type=tar on the client and remove the temporary container.
@mheon, since you mentioned preferring the existing Export() APIs, does this direction sound reasonable, or would you still prefer using images.Export() and reconstructing the rootfs client-side?
@shivaansh0610-LUFFY, are you still actively working on this? Happy to coordinate if you are.
